\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Reconstructed angular distributions obtained with the simulation algorithm accounting for experimental defects. Three representative states are illustrated, with predicted $l = 0$ or $l = 2$ shapes according to the panel title. In all cases, the reconstructed cross section identifies the predicted $l$ shape unambiguously, despite the uncertainty bars.\relax }}{8}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rec_xs}{{7}{8}{Reconstructed angular distributions obtained with the simulation algorithm accounting for experimental defects. Three representative states are illustrated, with predicted $l = 0$ or $l = 2$ shapes according to the panel title. In all cases, the reconstructed cross section identifies the predicted $l$ shape unambiguously, despite the uncertainty bars.\relax }{figure.caption.8}{}}
